WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:03.490
Welcome back to Curious Archive.

00:00:03.490 --> 00:00:08.340
This video is the second part of a two-part
series exploring the incredible speculative

00:00:08.340 --> 00:00:12.900
alien world of the Birrin, so check out part
I if you haven’t already.

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:18.039
The world of the Birrin was realized by Alex
Ries — an exceptional designer and worldbuilder

00:00:18.039 --> 00:00:23.259
who worked on the video game subnautica — and
I have links to where you can follow and support

00:00:23.259 --> 00:00:25.339
him in this video’s description.

00:00:25.339 --> 00:00:30.449
In part one, we broke down the biology and
early history of the Birrin, a six-limbed

00:00:30.449 --> 00:00:34.010
sentient alien race at the center of this
fictional world.

00:00:34.010 --> 00:00:35.879
But there’s still a lot to cover.

00:00:35.879 --> 00:00:41.590
Which is why, In this entry into the archive,
we’ll be chronicling the next several eons

00:00:41.590 --> 00:00:46.030
of Birrin history, following their incredible
arc into the far future.

00:00:46.030 --> 00:00:47.910
So, let’s get started.

00:00:47.910 --> 00:00:53.190
When we last saw the Birrin, their civilization
had undergone an apocalyptic reset back to

00:00:53.190 --> 00:00:58.350
the preindustrial era, due to an event called
‘The Fall’ — which turned the equatorial

00:00:58.350 --> 00:01:02.539
region of their planet into an inhospitable
wasteland known as ‘The Kiln.’

00:01:02.539 --> 00:01:07.910
This vast, super-heated region cut the Birrin
populations north and south of the area off

00:01:07.910 --> 00:01:08.910
from one another.

00:01:08.910 --> 00:01:14.940
And Birrin aren’t the only species on planet
Chriirah effected by the Fall.

00:01:14.940 --> 00:01:19.500
Organisms like the Irridalli, a group of unique
spear-faced predators that thrived in the

00:01:19.500 --> 00:01:25.270
tropical oceans, suffered a disastrous population
decline as their biome — and indeed, the

00:01:25.270 --> 00:01:26.980
entire planet — turned upside-down.

00:01:26.980 --> 00:01:32.790
But even after The Fall, many Birrin, though
bereft of certain technologies, continue to

00:01:32.790 --> 00:01:35.330
live relatively average lives.

00:01:35.330 --> 00:01:40.480
Some populations live as farmers of a plant-like
organism called Bluestick — essentially

00:01:40.480 --> 00:01:43.240
returning to agricultural societies.

00:01:43.240 --> 00:01:47.890
Although the lives of these post-Fall Bluestick
farmers are just a single, small blip in the

00:01:47.890 --> 00:01:53.050
vast history of the Birrin — Alex Ries has
mapped out every single aspect of the agricultural

00:01:53.050 --> 00:01:57.240
practice — making his fictional world feel
all the more palpable.

00:01:57.240 --> 00:02:02.340
This diagram showcases in detail how Birrin
Bluestick agriculture works.

00:02:02.340 --> 00:02:07.160
The Bluestick grows best alongside channels
of Brackish water: hence the design you see

00:02:07.160 --> 00:02:08.250
before you.

00:02:08.250 --> 00:02:13.390
Interestingly, the bluestick can’t photosynthesize,
but grow symbiotically with the red-tinted

00:02:13.390 --> 00:02:16.380
organism called Raftweed to produce food.

00:02:16.380 --> 00:02:19.610
Indeed, most of the plants on the Birrin world
are composites.

00:02:19.610 --> 00:02:24.840
Here, you can see the life cycle of the strange
tree-within-a-tree organisms that dot the

00:02:24.840 --> 00:02:27.120
landscapes of Bluestick farms.

00:02:27.120 --> 00:02:30.170
Once again, the level of detail here is impressive.

00:02:30.170 --> 00:02:35.040
The Bluestick plants are preyed upon by the
glassworms: a group of small, translucent

00:02:35.040 --> 00:02:36.040
pests.

00:02:36.040 --> 00:02:40.620
These creatures have evolved a specialized
hierarchy, and can be divided into queens,

00:02:40.620 --> 00:02:45.420
soldiers, and workers: much like the complex
social structures of ants here on earth.

00:02:45.420 --> 00:02:49.860
The glassworms are in turn preyed upon by
the Chattertails, which are greatly valued

00:02:49.860 --> 00:02:54.540
by Birrin Bluestick farmers thanks to their
natural pest control capabilities.

00:02:54.540 --> 00:02:59.630
Their alarming looking mouths are in fact
folded forelimbs used to ensnare prey.

00:02:59.630 --> 00:03:05.320
When the time is right, these sharp limbs
snap forward and ensnare the unlucky glassworms:

00:03:05.320 --> 00:03:07.870
keeping the bluestick crop safe from harm.

00:03:07.870 --> 00:03:13.160
Elsewhere on the Bluestick farm, we have the
thoroughly-detailed Bluestick Mill — a manufacturing

00:03:13.160 --> 00:03:16.810
structure that uses a large wind turbine to
power a mortar.

00:03:16.810 --> 00:03:21.870
The technology here is based on pre-fall designs
— showing that Birrin civilization isn’t

00:03:21.870 --> 00:03:23.860
quite starting from square-one.

00:03:23.860 --> 00:03:28.040
The Bluestick mill grinds the raw crops into
a concentrated gel.

00:03:28.040 --> 00:03:33.189
This processed Bluestick is profitable for
its medicinal, industrial, and chemical uses

00:03:33.189 --> 00:03:37.320
— especially now that older industries have
all but collapsed.

00:03:37.320 --> 00:03:41.920
Helping to farm these Bluestick fields are
groups of Giants, the second intelligent race

00:03:41.920 --> 00:03:46.599
on planet Chriirah who also suffered a population
decline due to The Fall.

00:03:46.599 --> 00:03:50.849
While giants and Birrin don’t always get
along, on this Bluestick farm, the Giants

00:03:50.849 --> 00:03:56.310
work alongside Birrin, as you can see here
with a group taking a well-deserved break.

00:03:56.310 --> 00:04:02.069
And there’s something about this image in
particular which captures strangely familiar

00:04:02.069 --> 00:04:04.050
and almost human emotions.

00:04:04.050 --> 00:04:07.180
But the pre-industrial reset wouldn’t last
forever.

00:04:07.180 --> 00:04:12.870
The Birrin technology which supported a space-faring
civilization, though forgotten and in ruins,

00:04:12.870 --> 00:04:15.860
was still out there, waiting to be rediscovered.

00:04:15.860 --> 00:04:20.939
Eventually, global shifts in the post-Fall
Birrin world reach the bluestick farm.

00:04:20.939 --> 00:04:26.500
Here, a motorized vehicle from an emerging
global power called the Reclamation arrives

00:04:26.500 --> 00:04:29.050
to assist the laborers in a gesture of goodwill.

00:04:29.050 --> 00:04:34.050
It’s a sign that after many centuries of
recovery, the world is being reborn.

00:04:34.050 --> 00:04:39.189
And over the course of the next era, the rebirth
following The Fall picked up speed.

00:04:39.189 --> 00:04:44.189
Eventually, the lethally warmed equator could
be navigated once more with the rediscovery

00:04:44.189 --> 00:04:45.189
of flight.

00:04:45.189 --> 00:04:51.439
Here, a primitive aircraft called the Kilnrunner
flies high over the expanse to avoid the searing

00:04:51.439 --> 00:04:52.439
heat.

00:04:52.439 --> 00:04:56.520
Crafts like this one help reconnect the north
and south Birrin populations for the first

00:04:56.520 --> 00:04:58.729
time in over a thousand years.

00:04:58.729 --> 00:05:03.199
In this next image, you can observe two Birrin
scaling the First Mountains — one of the

00:05:03.199 --> 00:05:07.270
few places on the planet that still possess
frigid temperatures.

00:05:07.270 --> 00:05:13.479
These explorers are another sign that, long
after the Fall, the world is starting to reconnect.

00:05:13.479 --> 00:05:19.749
One detail I especially like is their unique
suits come with mouth-operated multitools,

00:05:19.749 --> 00:05:24.479
since Birrin often use their beaks as well
as their front limbs when manipulating objects.

00:05:24.479 --> 00:05:29.910
In another scene showing the Birrin society
making impressive strides towards a more technologically

00:05:29.910 --> 00:05:35.439
advanced civilization, here, a Reclamation
heavy-lift delivers a wind turbine to the

00:05:35.439 --> 00:05:36.710
Birrin of a river valley.

00:05:36.710 --> 00:05:41.959
This image shows that long forgotten technology
is returning to the society of the Birrin

00:05:41.959 --> 00:05:44.479
— and the disparate populations are reconnecting
with each other more and more.

00:05:44.479 --> 00:05:49.270
Like any movement, however, the so-called
Reclamation is complicated.

00:05:49.270 --> 00:05:54.319
Many parts of the faction are more interested
in empire building than helping to rebuild.

00:05:54.319 --> 00:05:59.210
Indeed, one thing I like about the Birrin
world is that its history isn’t a straight

00:05:59.210 --> 00:06:02.380
line, but a long road of progress and backsliding.

00:06:02.380 --> 00:06:07.809
With the mistakes of past civilizations still
in many minds, however, overall the Birrin

00:06:07.809 --> 00:06:11.129
species would begin to move towards a better
tomorrow.

00:06:11.129 --> 00:06:16.830
Here, you can see a twin-mast Reclamation
ship coasting along the coast of the Tuktalli

00:06:16.830 --> 00:06:21.830
region, marveling at the ruins along the coastline
— which has not been seen for thousands

00:06:21.830 --> 00:06:22.900
of years due to the fall.

00:06:22.900 --> 00:06:27.530
Since the Tuktalli region is located deep
within the Kiln, it would have been inhospitable

00:06:27.530 --> 00:06:32.789
for quite some time.

00:06:32.789 --> 00:06:38.199
By now, Birrin society is at last entering
a second age of scientific advancement.

00:06:38.199 --> 00:06:43.169
Soon, more egalitarian reclamation efforts
would emerge on both sides of the Kiln.

00:06:43.169 --> 00:06:48.259
Here, a Birrin plane-like vehicle called the
cresting wave begins to make its ascent in

00:06:48.259 --> 00:06:54.349
front of a sustainable, gleaming city: showing
that the gloom of the Fall is truly lifting.

00:06:54.349 --> 00:06:58.949
Even more striking, in this image, you can
see the Birrin rediscover rocket technology

00:06:58.949 --> 00:07:02.789
through reverse engineering ancient, pre-Fall
designs.

00:07:02.789 --> 00:07:06.729
These rockets aren’t as effective as the
old ones, but advancements would continue

00:07:06.729 --> 00:07:11.629
throughout the next several centuries — as
Birrin technology ultimately advanced beyond

00:07:11.629 --> 00:07:12.939
that of their predecessors.

00:07:12.939 --> 00:07:19.309
Here, at an even later date, we can see the
space program has expanded, as a Birrin astronaut

00:07:19.309 --> 00:07:24.629
explores a nearby planet as part of the species’
first program to explore the further reaches

00:07:24.629 --> 00:07:26.529
of the Birrin solar system.

00:07:26.529 --> 00:07:31.759
Considering all the suffering the Birrin society
endured, it’s a stirring image of all they’ve

00:07:31.759 --> 00:07:32.759
overcome.

00:07:32.759 --> 00:07:38.819
Eventually, it’s possible the Birrin would
even encounter some future version of humanity.

00:07:38.819 --> 00:07:44.009
This image is no longer officially ‘canon’
according to Alex Ries — but it shows an

00:07:44.009 --> 00:07:49.229
intriguing possible future where technologically
advanced humans and Birrin study interactions

00:07:49.229 --> 00:07:53.669
between babies of both species to gather data
for a hypothetical joint colony.

00:07:53.669 --> 00:07:57.750
It’s a hypothetical idea I find very intriguing.

00:07:57.750 --> 00:08:03.310
But perhaps if the Birrin even encounter humanity,
it won’t be humanity as we know it.

00:08:03.310 --> 00:08:08.270
In this final, famous image from an unknown
point in the Birrin’s future, we see two

00:08:08.270 --> 00:08:13.469
Birrin meeting an awe-inspiring visitor simply
called the ‘meta-human.’

00:08:13.469 --> 00:08:19.319
Is this powerful being an artificial descendant
of humanity, several millennia into the future,

00:08:19.319 --> 00:08:24.409
at a time when our technology has turned us
into something we scarcely would recognize?

00:08:24.409 --> 00:08:28.349
That’s certainly my theory, although it’s
left up to interpretation.

00:08:28.349 --> 00:08:34.740
It’s an enigmatic image purposefully left
vague: a story which has yet to be told…

00:08:34.740 --> 00:08:39.529
In the end, the Birrin are both a cautionary
tale and an uplifting one.

00:08:39.529 --> 00:08:44.889
The story of a civilization that rose, and
fell, and rose again.

00:08:44.889 --> 00:08:50.440
If you liked this exploration, I’d encourage
you to check out more of the Birrin on Alex

00:08:50.440 --> 00:08:55.380
Ries’s own page: there are extra details
on his site, including his creative process

00:08:55.380 --> 00:08:57.870
behind some of these images.

00:08:57.870 --> 00:09:00.069
Once again, links are in the description.

00:09:00.069 --> 00:09:04.380
Like I said in part I, Alex Ries is also planning
to release a full book about this incredible

00:09:04.380 --> 00:09:07.670
world sometime in the future, so stay tuned
for that!

00:09:07.670 --> 00:09:09.380
Also, thanks for watching.

00:09:09.380 --> 00:09:14.380
If you enjoyed this entry, please lend your
support and like, subscribe, and hit the notification

00:09:14.380 --> 00:09:17.790
icon to stay up to date on all things Curious.

00:09:17.790 --> 00:09:19.000
See you in the next video.

